---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Plugins · MindContext — Constellation" description="The future MindContext plugin model: explicit capabilities, portable Markdown and no raw storage credentials.">
  <div class="content-shell">
    <PageHero eyebrow="PLUGINS · IN DEVELOPMENT" title="Extend MindContext without surrendering your vault." description="The plugin ecosystem is a future direction. The architecture already separates plugin capabilities from storage-provider credentials." />

    <section class="content-grid three">
      <article class="content-card"><span class="feature-icon">⌘</span><h2>Commands</h2><p>Future plugins can contribute discoverable commands and workflows to the shared command model.</p><small>Architecture seam exists</small></article>
      <article class="content-card"><span class="feature-icon">◇</span><h2>Views</h2><p>Add focused ways to project knowledge without turning those projections into canonical storage.</p><small>Future capability</small></article>
      <article class="content-card"><span class="feature-icon">↔</span><h2>Integrations</h2><p>Connect tools through explicit permissions instead of handing third-party code raw Drive credentials.</p><small>Future capability</small></article>
    </section>

    <section class="prose-section">
      <h2>Plugin principles</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Markdown and ordinary files stay canonical.</li>
        <li>Capabilities are explicit and least-privilege.</li>
        <li>Plugins do not receive raw storage-provider credentials.</li>
        <li>Core workflows continue to function without community plugins.</li>
        <li>A plugin should be removable without trapping the user's knowledge.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="plugin-roadmap">
      <article><span>NOW</span><h3>Plugin-ready boundaries</h3><p>Shared extension vocabulary and command registration seams exist in the repository.</p></article>
      <article><span>NEXT</span><h3>Core extension surfaces</h3><p>Harden commands, views and safe data access before exposing broad third-party execution.</p></article>
      <article><span>LATER</span><h3>Community ecosystem</h3><p>Discovery, packaging, trust and permissions need deliberate product design before a marketplace.</p></article>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
